*******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
*** PART J: Further robustness of the headline effect (reviewer checks)
***   J1 health block in M11: joint Wald test of self-rated health and activity limitation
***   J2 M12 estimated on the M11 sample (difference M12 vs. M11 not driven by the few cases dropped in M11)
***   J3 flexible income control instead of the linear income position in M12:
***      J3a income bands (< 40, 40-60, 60-80, >= 80 % of the poverty line), J3b restricted cubic spline (4 knots),
***      J3c common income range: only persons between 50 and 100 % of the poverty line
***   J4 R4 AROP w/o IWP without persons currently employed at the interview (act_status == 1)
***   J5 wealth proxies (EU-SILC has no wealth variable): M13a = M12 + tenure (HH021);
***      M13 = M13a + capital income (HY090G > 0) + rental income (HY040G > 0); M13h = M13 + health
***      capital income is close to the outcome (savings <-> coping with unexpected expenses) -> M13a is the main variant
***   J6 SMSD without the arrears item (12 items, >= 7 lacking): tenure mechanically affects mortgage/rent arrears
*******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************

di _n(2) as result "=================== PART J: Further robustness ==================="

